                <pb facs="0388" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163 American Church Mission/12:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-18T13:00:00-05:00">November 18, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. Reference Nanking’s 908, November 12, noon. The Department suggests that
                    unless you perceive objection you make appropriate representations to the
                    Japanese Foreign Office on the basis of the telegram under reference.</p>
                <p>For your information the Department has received an inquiry from the mission
                    headquarters, New York, in regard to this case.</p>
                <p>Please report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
